tched)"},{"type":"text","text":" from a CloudKit re-hydrate action)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In-memory state may hold unflushed writes or live UI bindings; wholesale"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replacement silently drops them and surfaces as lost keystrokes. Use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/merge(from:shouldReplace:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for that path — it records no changes and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lets you decide per-ID which side wins. Under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentCloudKitContainer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the gotcha is especially sharp: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".NSPersistentStoreRemoteChange"},{"type":"text","text":" fires for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local saves too, so a naïve “refresh on remote change” observer feeds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app its own writes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entities sharing an ID are collapsed to the first occurrence. A store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cannot represent duplicates — ","type":"text"},{"code":"positions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds one index per ID — and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"admitting them corrupts the index: the map would keep only the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index while the array kept every copy, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over-reports and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"later delete orphans the earlier copy with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"positions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry at all,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaving a row that is visible in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/S